  "details": "Single physbones with an angle limit look great when stretching the physbone; but when trying to squish it, the physbone always squirms away from the pushing source, causing it to flip around jitteringly, instead of being squished into place.  It would be good if physbones could have an option to reduce their angle limit range down towards zero as the squishedness increases, so that squishing contact will drive them towards their origin rather than away from it.",
